<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n11172" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Corfīnĭum</span></b> , ii,
			n., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Κορφίνιον</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a very strongly
				fortified town of the Peligni, north of Sulmo</i>, now <i>Pelino</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. Att. 8,
				3, 7</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Caes. B. C. 1, 15 sq.</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Luc. 2,
				478 al.</span></i>—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Corfīnĭensis</span></b> , e, <i>adj., of</i> or <i>pertaining to
				Corfinium</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">clementia,</span>”
				i. e. <i>exercised by Cæsar at this city</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Att. 9, 16, 1</span></i>
			; cf. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">exspectatio,</span>”
				i. e. <i>of occurrences there</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 8, 5, 2</span></i>
			.—In plur.: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Corfīnĭenses</span></b> ,
			ium, m., <i>the inhabitants
				of Corfinium</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 3, 12, 17, §
			106</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Corfīnĭus</span></b> ,
				a, um, <i>adj., of Corfinium</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ager,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Front. Colon. p. 122</span></i>
			 Goes.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
